# money-vault-announce-v1 (kind 7): the recovery authority announces a new policy; it applies after the
# recovery delay unless cancelled. The announcement reveals the OLD policy hash, which the node revokes in
# the announcing block (F-799: a pending withdrawal under the old policy is revoked at the announcement,
# not at the recovery's completion, so the revocation binds inside D; a cancelled recovery restores it).
# The everyday key may co-sign the announcement (F-800: a rotation of the cancellation key that the owner's
# everyday key co-signed is cancellable by the recovery authority alone; one without the co-signature by the
# cancellation key, so a compromised authority's rotation is still the owner's to cancel); the co-signature
# bit is carried in the head's IDX word (element 3) for the cancellation statement to read.
# Public: DOMAIN [chain_id, 7, 0, 0], ANCHOR, NF_HEAD, CM_HEAD_OUT, OLD_POLICY_HASH, HT = [h_decl, t_decl, 0, 0].
# Advice, in the order read: the six public words; the policy's eight words; SK_A; NK_V; head_in (V, VID,
# IDX, SPENT, RECH, R, pos); the co-signature bit; when set, SK_E and NK_E; the new policy's eight words;
# head_out's R.
# The circuit: the policy hashes to the revealed word and is the head's; pk_a = H(SK_A, TAG 17), not all-zero;
# the head is in the tree; no recovery pending; the bit is 0 or 1 and, when 1, pk_e = H(SK_E, NK_E); the new
# policy meets the floors; head_out = head_in with rec_hash = new_policy_hash, rec_h = h_decl, rec_t = t_decl,
# IDX element 3 = the bit.
begin
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.0
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.4 swapw hmerge
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.8 swapw hmerge
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.12 swapw hmerge
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.16 swapw hmerge
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.20 swapw hmerge
    dupw.1 assert_eqw
    mem_load.1 push.7 assert_eq
    padw mem_loadw_le.20 u32assertw dropw
    exec.read_policy
    push.100 exec.hash_policy
    padw mem_loadw_le.132 padw mem_loadw_le.16 assert_eqw
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.272 dropw
    push.0.0.0.17 padw mem_loadw_le.272 hmerge
    padw mem_loadw_le.108 assert_eqw
    padw mem_loadw_le.108 exec.word_is_zero not assert
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.176 dropw
    exec.check_nk_field
    exec.open_head
    padw mem_loadw_le.160 exec.word_is_zero assert
    adv_push dup.0 dup.0 mul dup.1 assert_eq
    dup.0 mem_store.420
    if.true
        padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.260 dropw
        padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.264 dropw
        padw mem_loadw_le.264 padw mem_loadw_le.260 hmerge
        padw mem_loadw_le.100 assert_eqw
    end
    exec.read_new_policy
    push.300 exec.check_floors
    push.300 exec.hash_policy
    push.180 push.140 exec.copy_word
    push.184 push.144 exec.copy_word
    push.188 push.132 exec.copy_word
    mem_load.152 mem_store.192
    mem_load.20 mem_store.193
    mem_load.21 mem_store.194
    mem_load.420 mem_store.195
    push.196 push.156 exec.copy_word
    push.200 push.332 exec.copy_word
    padw adv_loadw mem_storew_le.204 dropw
    push.180 exec.hash_head
    padw mem_loadw_le.208 padw mem_loadw_le.12 assert_eqw
end
